Whether the rally seen in the previous session can sustain itself will be key to watch in the coming sessions. Although the broader market structure remains weak, momentum indicators have shown signs of strength. If the Nifty 50 manages to defend its immediate support at 22,600, its 10-day (EMA), it could move towards 22,800 and then 23,000, despite the possibility of some consolidation. However, a break below 22,600 could expose the index to further downside, with the 22,300–22,200 zone acting as a crucial support area. Meanwhile, the Bank Nifty needs to hold support at 55,400 and 55,100 to avoid potential selling pressure. On the upside, resistance is placed at 56,100 and 56,500, experts said.
