On the hourly chart, prices have moved above the 89 EMA for the first time since the August decline, a positive sign for the bulls, as earlier any bounce towards this was getting sold into. The RSI also supports the improving setup. After showing positive divergence, it has broken out of a double bottom and moved above 40, a level that typically acts as resistance during bear market bounces. This suggests a likely shift in momentum.
Notably, these positive formations are emerging right at the long-term support of the 200-week EMA, raising the probability of further upside in the near term. On an immediate basis, prices may retest the 20-day EMA around 22,900–23,000, and a move above this could extend the rally towards the 50-day EMA at 23,600.
Traders are advised to remain buoyant and use dips as buying opportunities. On the downside, 22,500 followed by 22,200 remain strong supports.
